---
title: "Memory: learning after a turn"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Start
    lg1: Learn
    lg2: Compress
    lg3: End
  }
  class lg0 blue
  class lg1 purple
  class lg2 teal
  class lg3 yellow
  s0: Turn saved, memory task starts
  s1: Recording use of recalled memories
  s2: Reading the owner's memory switch
  s3: Extracting facts with the extractor model
  s4: Finished, every failure only logged
  s5: Embedding and reconciling with similar memories
  s6: Looking for old groups to summarize
  s7: Summarizing one group
  s8: Storing facts, marking the ones they replace
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: the turn used memories
  s0 --> s2: the turn used none
  s1 --> s2: use count and last use updated
  s2 --> s4: switch off, or the read fails
  s2 --> s3: switch on
  s3 --> s5: facts found
  s3 --> s6: no new facts, or the extractor fails
  s5 --> s6: every fact already known
  s5 --> s8: new or replacing facts [all kept if the reconciler fails]
  s6 --> s4: no group due
  s6 --> s7: a group of 2+ memories older than 7 days [3 per turn]
  s7 --> s6: summary replaces the group, or the group is kept
  s8 --> s6: stored, or the store fails
  class s0 blue
  class s1 blue
  class s2 blue
  class s3 purple
  class s4 yellow
  class s5 purple
  class s6 teal
  class s7 teal
  class s8 purple
